         TITLE 'MPMCQ SAM64 copy helpers (31-bit buffers <-> 64-bit payload)'
***********************************************************************
*  MPMCQ_COPY64.MAC
*
*  Copy helpers used by QENQ/QDEQ to move variable-length data between:
*  - 31-bit caller buffers (AMODE 31 addressability)
*  - 64-bit virtual storage payload buffers (IARV64)
*
*  Implementation approach:
*  - Switch to 64-bit addressing mode briefly using SAM64/SAM31.
*  - Use MVCL with register pairs.
*
*  Register conventions for macros below:
*  - Destination pair: &RDST / &RDST+1  (address / length)
*  - Source pair:      &RSRC / &RSRC+1  (address / length)
*
*  Notes:
*  - Caller must ensure upper bits of any 31-bit addresses are zero.
*  - MVCL will pad with X'00' if source shorter than destination; we always
*    set both lengths to the same value to avoid padding effects.
***********************************************************************

         MACRO
&LBL     MPMCQ_COPY_31_TO_64 &SRC31,&DST64,&LEN,&RDST,&RSRC,&RWORK
* Copy LEN bytes from 31-bit SRC31 to 64-bit DST64.
* Inputs:
*  - &SRC31 : register containing 31-bit source address (upper cleared)
*  - &DST64 : even reg containing 64-bit destination address
*  - &LEN   : register containing length (fullword, <=2G-1)
* Clobbers:
*  - &RDST/&RDST+1, &RSRC/&RSRC+1, &RWORK
&L       SETC  '&LBL'
         AIF   ('&LBL' NE '').C3164_HAVE
&L       SETC  'C3&SYSNDX'                 * <=8 chars
.C3164_HAVE ANOP
&L.      LGR   &RDST,&DST64
         LR    &RDST+1,&LEN
         LLGTR &RSRC,&SRC31
         LR    &RSRC+1,&LEN
         SAM64
         MVCL  &RDST,&RSRC
         SAM31
         MEND

         MACRO
&LBL     MPMCQ_COPY_64_TO_31 &SRC64,&DST31,&LEN,&RDST,&RSRC,&RWORK
* Copy LEN bytes from 64-bit SRC64 to 31-bit DST31.
* Inputs:
*  - &SRC64 : even reg containing 64-bit source address
*  - &DST31 : register containing 31-bit destination address (upper cleared)
*  - &LEN   : register containing length (fullword, <=2G-1)
* Clobbers:
*  - &RDST/&RDST+1, &RSRC/&RSRC+1, &RWORK
&L       SETC  '&LBL'
         AIF   ('&LBL' NE '').C6431_HAVE
&L       SETC  'C6&SYSNDX'                 * <=8 chars
.C6431_HAVE ANOP
&L.      LLGTR &RDST,&DST31
         LR    &RDST+1,&LEN
         LGR   &RSRC,&SRC64
         LR    &RSRC+1,&LEN
         SAM64
         MVCL  &RDST,&RSRC
         SAM31
         MEND

* (end of file)

